# ALTN 1 FAIL: alternator 1 gives no current and the main bus runs on the battery (format 1). The checklist (heading, message, rows and comment rows) is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05 (owner decision 2026-10-23); all other text is own wording. The threshold, hold time, onset window and forbidden items are instructor-review values.
format: 1
id: elec-altn1-fail
title: ALTN 1 FAIL
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: AFM 03A-02 ALTN 1 FAIL
  verified: "2026-10-23"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: cruise
briefing:
  situation: "You are in cruise flight when the yellow ALTN 1 FAIL message appears on the primary flight display. The alternator 1 Amps reading has dropped to zero. The engine runs normally and the main bus now draws on the battery."
initial:
  quantities:
    alt1_amps: 0
    alt1_fault: 1
    bus_volts: 25.9
    battery_pct: 98
parameters:
  alt1_output: 0
annunciations[1]: altn_1_fail
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: ALTN 1 FAIL
  message: ALTERNATOR 1 HAS FAILED
procedure[5]:
  - kind: group
    id: breaker_check
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: alt1_breaker_in
        severity: critical
        number: 1
        text: Circuit breaker
        action: check IN
        done:
          check: state
          control: cb.alt1
          is: in
  - kind: group
    id: immediate
    ordered: false
    steps[2]:
      - id: alt1_off
        severity: critical
        number: 2
        text: Alternator 1
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.alternator_1
          is: off
      - id: ess_bus_on
        severity: critical
        number: 3
        text: Essential bus
        action: "ON"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.ess_bus
          is: on
  - kind: line
    number: 4
    text: Bus voltage
    action: MONITOR
  - kind: comment
    text: Terminate NVFR/IFR-flight and land at nearest suitable airfield.
  - kind: comment
    text: Leave icing conditions.
# Each of these removes the remaining supply of the bus; both are instructor-review items.
forbidden[2]:
  - id: alt2_off
    text: Switch off alternator 2
    fails_run: true
    trigger:
      check: state
      control: sw.alternator_2
      is: off
  - id: elect_master_off
    text: Switch off the electrical master
    fails_run: true
    trigger:
      check: state
      control: sw.elect_master
      is: off
# The outcome ends the run as a fail when the bus voltage stays at the battery floor; the voltage and the hold time are instructor-review values.
outcomes[1]:
  - id: main_bus_lost
    text: Total loss of main bus power
    hold_s: 10
    when:
      check: quantity
      quantity: bus_volts
      op: lte
      value: 22.5
# The four causes behind the one message (phase 3.1): the alternator is dead and the breaker in; the breaker has popped and the alternator is fine; the alternator has a short and its breaker pops again when it is pushed in; the breaker has popped and the alternator is dead too, so pushing it in does not help. The checklist above is the printed one; which of its rows are graded depends on the cause drawn at the start of a run. The weights and the cause texts are instructor-review values.
variants[4]:
  - id: alternator_dead
    weight: 40
    applies[2]: alt1_off,ess_bus_on
    debrief: The breaker was in and alternator 1 had failed.
  - id: breaker_popped
    weight: 30
    controls:
      cb.alt1: out
    parameters:
      alt1_output: 1
    applies[1]: alt1_breaker_in
    debrief: The alternator 1 circuit breaker had popped. Pushing it in cleared the message.
  - id: alternator_shorted
    weight: 15
    controls:
      cb.alt1: out
    parameters:
      alt1_short: 1
    applies[2]: alt1_off,ess_bus_on
    debrief: Alternator 1 had a short and its circuit breaker had popped. Pushing the breaker in only popped it again, so the alternator had to be switched off.
  - id: breaker_popped_dead
    weight: 15
    controls:
      cb.alt1: out
    applies[2]: alt1_off,ess_bus_on
    debrief: The alternator 1 circuit breaker had popped and the alternator was dead as well. Pushing the breaker in did not help.
# The failure of the level Realistic begins at a random second inside this short window; the window is an instructor-review value.
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
